  <section class="academy-detail-hero wrap interview-detail"><div class="detail-heading"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> PATH 02 / EXPLAIN</div><h1>Interview<br /><em>Notes.</em></h1><p>Knowing a term is the beginning. Explaining how it works, why it matters, and where it breaks is the skill. These planned notes will make that progression explicit.</p><div class="detail-tags"><span>QUESTION LED</span><span>DEEP EXPLANATIONS</span><span>FOLLOW UPS</span></div><div class="detail-status"><span class="academy-status">IN DEVELOPMENT</span><span>Study packs are not available yet.</span></div></div><div class="question-preview"><div class="question-preview-top"><span>FORMAT PREVIEW / 001</span><span>Q → A → WHY</span></div><div class="question-preview-main"><span class="question-preview-label">SAMPLE QUESTION</span><h2>What is the difference between authentication and authorization?</h2><div class="preview-answer"><span>SHORT ANSWER</span><p>Authentication establishes who a principal is. Authorization determines what that principal may access or do.</p></div><div class="preview-follow"><span>GO DEEPER</span><p>How do group membership, access tokens, and resource permissions turn that distinction into a real access decision?</p></div></div><div class="question-preview-foot">EXAMPLE OF THE PLANNED NOTE STRUCTURE <span>↗</span></div></div></section>
  <section class="academy-detail-section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-kicker">THE NOTE FORMAT / 01</div><h2>Answer. Explain. Connect<span class="title-stop">.</span></h2></div><p>Each planned note will move from an interview sized response to the mechanics and follow ups that reveal real understanding.</p></div><div class="detail-feature-grid interview-features"><div><span>01 / ANSWER</span><h3>The clear version</h3><p>A concise, accurate answer you can say aloud without hiding behind jargon.</p></div><div><span>02 / MECHANICS</span><h3>The deeper model</h3><p>Diagrams, examples, and system behavior that explain why the answer holds.</p></div><div><span>03 / FOLLOW UP</span><h3>The next question</h3><p>Likely extensions, edge cases, and tradeoffs to test the strength of your understanding.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="academy-modules wrap"><div class="academy-modules-intro"><span>PLANNED QUESTION AREAS / 02</span><h2>Organized by the systems behind the questions.</h2><p>These are proposed study areas, not currently published packs.</p></div><div class="module-list"><div><span>AREA / 01</span><h3>Active Directory & identity</h3><p>Domains, authentication, authorization, Kerberos, delegation, and trust.</p><b>→</b></div><div><span>AREA / 02</span><h3>Linux environments</h3><p>Users, permissions, processes, services, logs, and system investigation.</p><b>→</b></div><div><span>AREA / 03</span><h3>Security reasoning</h3><p>Threat models, evidence, prioritization, reporting, and communicating uncertainty.</p><b>→</b></div></div></section>
